    "method": "Joint inversion of ascending and descending Sentinel-1 interferograms and ARKL GNSS displacements. The paper first solved for a uniform rectangular fault and then for spatially variable slip on 1.5 x 1.5 km patches with smoothing. This JSON digitizes the published Figure 8 perspective view.",
    "green_function_model": "Elastic rectangular dislocations in a homogeneous half-space (Okada-type geodetic inversion framework).",
    "slip_type": "variable",
    "smoothing_constraint": true,
    "notes": "Perspective-view digitization of Figure 8 (page 14). The published fault plane is 13.4 x 10.5 km, strike 195 deg, dip 55 deg, top depth 1.2 km, and was subdivided into 1.5 x 1.5 km constant-slip patches, implying a 9 x 7 grid. Because the published panel is oblique/perspective, cell boundaries were interpreted after mentally rectifying the plane; values are approximate class/contour-based estimates read from the printed colour scale (0-120 cm) rather than original inversion coefficients. Maximum published slip is about 1.2 m at ~4.9-6.2 km depth. Geographic coordinates for individual patches are not explicitly printed and are left null."
  },
